__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.git
.venv
venv/
papers/
output/
*.csv
*.json
# The hosted API serves these cached answers (see
# generate_demo_answer_cache.py) and needs the production graph CSVs for
# the --kg fallback -- negations must come after the excludes above.
!data/demo_answer_cache.json
!data/production_graph/*.csv

# Flutter build state. Dockerfile.web compiles the frontend inside the image,
# so a laptop's build output and tool cache are both irrelevant and large --
# and shipping a stale build/web into the context invites confusion about
# which bundle is being served. Verified 2026-10-28 that the `*.json` and
# `*.csv` lines above do NOT reach nested paths (Docker matches patterns
# against the whole relative path, and `*` does not cross a separator), so
# flutter_application/web/manifest.json still reaches the build.
flutter_application/build/
flutter_application/.dart_tool/
